      "side": 1,
      "message": "If my understanding is correct, PMIC cuts off ec\u0027s VCC power rail through i2c commands in this case. If so, it should have no harm without calling __enter_hibernate. And it\u0027s better to add an infinite loop at the end of board_hibernate() in case ec has a chance to execute few instructions in __enter_hibernate(). \n\nRegarding system_enter_psl_mode(), setting bit 5 of PDOUT(8) will pull  PSL_OUT (GPIO85) to low. Once ec received PSL input event, PSL_OUT will be pulled to high immediately. Does this pin influence the ROP PMIC? Or ec won\u0027t wake-up from hibernating.",
